    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50712" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱππηλά̆τ-ης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>driver of horses, one who fights from a chariot</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> (always in 
				Ep.
			 from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱππηλάτα</span>, and only
			in nom.), as an epith. of honour, <u>Knight</u>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱ. Τυδεύς, γέρων ἱ. Πηλεύς, Φοῖνιξ,
				Οἰνεύς</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				4.387
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				7.125
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				9.432
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				581
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νέστωρ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					3.436
				</span></i>
			: generally 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱππηλάται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					E.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					117
				</span></i>
			: as Adj., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἱ.
			λεώς</span>, opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πεδοστιβής</span>,
				<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				126
			</span></i> (lyr.).</div>
